        "customColor": "#7c3aed",
        "designMd": "# Design System Document: The Celestial Nexus\n\n## 1. Overview & Creative North Star\n**Creative North Star: \"The Cosmic Architect\"**\n\nThis design system is not a website; it is an interface into a digital void. It rejects the \"boxy\" constraints of traditional web design in favor of an immersive, cinematic experience that feels like a high-end command deck at the edge of the universe. \n\nTo break the \"template\" look, we utilize **intentional asymmetry** and **overlapping geometry**. Elements should feel as though they are orbiting a central gravity well, with large-scale typography bleeding off-canvas and \"Stellar\" accents providing light in a vast, dark expanse. This is a balance of brutalist geometry (the display type) and ethereal softness (the glassmorphism and glows).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Colors & Atmospheric Depth\nOur palette is rooted in the deep obsidian of space, using light not as a decoration, but as a functional tool for navigation.\n\n### The Palette (Material Design Tokens)\n- **Primary (Nebula Violet):** `#d2bbff` / `#7c3aed` — Used for high-priority actions and \"core energy\" elements.\n- **Secondary (Stellar Cyan):** `#5de6ff` / `#22d3ee` — Reserved for technical indicators, active states, and interactive feedback.\n- **Tertiary (Solar Gold):** `#ffb95f` / `#f59e0b` — Used sparingly for \"critical\" highlights, awards, or unique CTA moments to mimic a solar corona.\n- **Surface & Background:** Base is `surface` (`#0c141e`).\n\n### The \"No-Line\" Rule\n**Explicit Instruction:** You are prohibited from using 1px solid borders to section off content. \nStructure must be defined through:\n1.  **Background Shifts:** Transitioning from `surface` to `surface-container-low`.\n2.  **Negative Space:** Using the Spacing Scale to create \"voids\" between content blocks.\n3.  **Glow Thresholds:** Defining an edge through a soft `primary_container` radial gradient.\n\n### Surface Hierarchy & Nesting\nTreat the UI as stacked sheets of synthetic material floating in a vacuum.\n- **Deepest:** `surface_container_lowest` (#070e19) for the global background.\n- **Mid-Tier:** `surface_container` (#19202b) for secondary content areas.\n- **Highest/Floating:** `surface_bright` (#323a46) for active cards or modals.\n*Nesting Example:* A `surface_container_high` card should only ever sit on a `surface_container_low` background to ensure a soft, natural luminance shift.\n\n### The \"Glass & Gradient\" Rule\nMain containers must utilize **Dark Glassmorphism**:\n- `background`: `rgba(25, 32, 43, 0.6)`\n- `backdrop-filter`: `blur(20px) saturate(150%)`\n- **Signature Texture:** Apply a subtle `radial-gradient` (top-left) using `primary` at 5% opacity to give the \"glass\" a tinted, premium feel.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Typography: The Editorial Scale\nWe contrast the rigid, \"machine-made\" display fonts with soft, readable humanist body copy.\n\n- **Display (Space Grotesk / Orbitron):** High-contrast, wide tracking (+5% to +10%). Use `display-lg` for hero statements. It should feel architectural.\n- **Headline/Title (Space Grotesk):** Sharp and authoritative. Use `headline-md` for section starters.\n- **Body (Be Vietnam Pro / Outfit):** Set in `body-md` for maximum legibility against the dark background. Ensure line-height is generous (1.6+) to prevent \"text-cramping\" in the dark theme.\n- **Labels (Fira Code):** Use for technical specs, dates, and \"code-like\" metadata. Always uppercase with increased letter spacing.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Elevation & Depth: Tonal Layering\nTraditional shadows do not exist in deep space. We use **Ambient Luminance**.\n\n- **The Layering Principle:** Depth is achieved by stacking surface tiers. If an element needs to feel \"closer\" to the user, increase its surface brightness, do not just add a black shadow.\n- **Ambient Shadows:** For floating elements, use a shadow color tinted with `primary` (`#7c3aed` at 8% opacity) with a blur radius of 40px+. This mimics the way a nebula would cast light around an object.\n- **The \"Ghost Border\" Fallback:** If a container requires an edge for accessibility, use `outline_variant` at **15% opacity**. It should be felt, not seen.\n- **Solar Corona Glows:** Use `tertiary_container` with a high blur (80px-120px) as a background element behind primary cards to create a \"stellar\" silhouette.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Components & Interface Elements\n\n### Buttons\n- **Primary:** No solid background. Use a `primary` to `primary_container` linear gradient with white text (`on_primary`).\n- **Secondary:** Transparent background with a \"Ghost Border\" (15% opacity `outline`). On hover, the border opacity increases to 100%.\n- **Tertiary:** Text only in `secondary`, using `label-md` (Fira Code) to emphasize the technical nature of the portfolio.\n\n### Cards & Lists\n- **The \"No-Divider\" Rule:** Never use `<hr>` or border-bottom. Separate list items using a 16px gap and a slight `surface_container_highest` background on hover.\n- **Interactive Cards:** On hover, a card should not move \"up\" (Y-axis). Instead, increase the `backdrop-filter` blur and slightly increase the opacity of the internal radial gradient.\n\n### Input Fields\n- **Styling:** Minimalist. Only a bottom-border using `outline_variant` at 30% opacity. \n- **Focus State:** The border transitions to `secondary` (Cyan), and a subtle `secondary` outer glow (4px blur) appears.\n\n### Signature Component: The \"Nebula Tracker\"\nA custom scroll indicator or cursor follower that uses a `primary` to `secondary` radial gradient with `filter: blur(40px)`. It sits behind the content (Z-index: -1) and follows the user's movement, subtly illuminating the \"glass\" sections as they pass over.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Do’s and Don’ts\n\n### Do:\n- **Do** use asymmetrical margins (e.g., 10% left, 20% right) to create an editorial, non-grid feel.\n- **Do** allow typography to overlap with subtle cosmic background animations.\n- **Do** use `primary_fixed_dim` for text on dark surfaces to reduce eye strain compared to pure white.\n\n### Don’t:\n- **Don’t** use pure black (#000000). Always use the `surface` tokens to maintain depth.\n- **Don’t** use \"pop\" animations. Use \"drift\" animations (slow, ease-in-out transforms) to mimic zero-gravity.\n- **Don’t** use high-contrast borders. If the design feels \"flat,\" adjust the `surface-container` tier rather than adding a line.\n- **Don't** use standard icons. Use thin-stroke (1px or 1.5px) geometric icons that match the `outline` token.",
